{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773763649,"nonce":"PHvDUk6zJ2HM5riEqK8PTcmnoGk=","title":"Per-repo workflow file discovery","message":"Currently nightshift assumes WORKFLOW.md in the repo root. Multi-repo setups (e.g. a docs repo alongside a code repo) need different workflow configs but require --workflow on every command.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. **nightshift init --workflow-path \u003cpath\u003e** — scaffold the workflow file at a custom location (e.g. ~/.config/nightshift/leanaider-docs.yaml)\n\n2. **Per-repo workflow pointer** — a local config that tells nightshift where to find the workflow file for this repo, so plain nightshift status / nightshift start just works. Two options (implement one):\n   - Option A: .nightshift.yaml in repo root with workflow: /path/to/workflow.yaml\n   - Option B: git config entry nightshift.workflow /path/to/workflow.yaml (stored in .git/config)\n\n3. **Discovery order** (first match wins):\n   - --workflow \u003cpath\u003e CLI flag (existing, highest priority)\n   - .nightshift.yaml in repo root (or git config entry)\n   - WORKFLOW.md in repo root (current default, lowest priority)\n\n## Use case\n\n- Code repo: WORKFLOW.md with pytest, code-focused prompts — works as today\n- Docs repo: workflow at ~/.config/nightshift/leanaider-docs.yaml with no test_command, canvas-aware prompts\n- nightshift start \u003cissue\u003e in either repo finds the right workflow automatically\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- host/cli.py: workflow discovery logic in every command that loads config\n- host/cli.py: nightshift init --workflow-path flag\n- host/launch.py: use discovery logic instead of hardcoded WORKFLOW.md\n- host/watcher/main.py: use discovery logic\n- Shared helper: extract workflow discovery to a function (e.g. host/config_discovery.py or host/env.py)\n\n## Tests needed\n\n- Discovery order: CLI flag \u003e .nightshift.yaml \u003e WORKFLOW.md\n- init --workflow-path creates file at custom location and writes .nightshift.yaml pointer\n- All commands use discovered workflow path\n- Missing workflow gives clear error message\n\nREQ-011","files":null}]}